{"availability":"available","full":"cyberchriz/musictools","name":"musictools","description":"Tonnetz Pro: A free, offline-capable, multitrack browser DAW and isomorphic synthesizer built with the Web Audio API","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":6,"forks":2,"created":"2026-04-01T13:15:21Z","updated":"2026-05-18T21:06:14Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://cyberchriz.github.io/musictools/index.html","topics":["circle-of-fifths","daw","drum-machine","harmony","keyboard","looper","midi-controller","music","music-theory","piano","pwa","synthesizer","tonnetz","web-audio-api"],"demo":"https://cyberchriz.github.io/musictools/index.html","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T20:31:56.714Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T20:31:56.714Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T20:31:56.714Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T13:58:50.266Z","stars":6,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-10T23:18:22.385Z","stars":6,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-16T20:31:56.714Z","stars":6,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A Digital Audio Workstation (DAW) and music theory tool with synthesizer and live performance environment all wrapped around Euler's \"Tonnetz\".","The \"Tonnetz\" concept is much more than eye-candy: it maps harmonic relationships to physical space, allowing for the intuitive visualization and application of complex chord structures. By translating musical intervals into a two-dimensional grid, users can explore tonal gravity, voice leading, and advanced chord extensions using visual memory rather than traditional linear keyboard mapping.","The good news for those who are still unfamiliar with the \"Tonnetz\" concept: the app is still fully usable as a traditional DAW. In other words: the Tonnetz chart is meant to rather be a useful tool, but by no means a prerequisite to get going with this app. Just plug in your MIDI controller or use the on-screen keyboard to start creating music immediately."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cyberchriz/musictools/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f1e0a2fdecc0be727c689f2840c0b612a0d9f069d18ff5d333bf1ff81b1bc181","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T13:58:50.424Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T13:58:50.424Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A Digital Audio Workstation (DAW) and music theory tool with synthesizer and live performance environment all wrapped around Euler's \"Tonnetz\".","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cyberchriz/musictools/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"f1e0a2fdecc0be727c689f2840c0b612a0d9f069d18ff5d333bf1ff81b1bc181","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cyberchriz/musictools/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T13:58:50.424Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-05-18T21:06:14Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cyberchriz/musictools/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T13:58:50.424Z","hash":"f1e0a2fdecc0be727c689f2840c0b612a0d9f069d18ff5d333bf1ff81b1bc181","originalBytes":14118,"storedBytes":14118,"truncated":false},"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T13:58:50.266Z","subjects":["Browser extensions & PWAs","Music & audio"],"platforms":[],"classification":{"version":4,"method":"local_rules","category":"Developer tools","subjects":["Browser extensions & PWAs","Music & audio"],"evidence":[{"subject":"Browser extensions & PWAs","source":"metadata","match":"pwa"},{"subject":"Music & audio","source":"metadata","match":"synthesizer"}],"platformEvidence":[],"platformSupport":"author_metadata_not_runtime_tested","suggestedSubjects":["Automation & workflows","Mobile","Maths & algorithms","Data & dashboards"],"reviewRequired":true},"demoHealth":{"url":"https://cyberchriz.github.io/musictools/index.html","attemptedAt":"2026-10-15T15:15:13.098Z","probeVersion":3,"status":"working","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T15:15:13.098Z","lastWorkingAt":"2026-10-15T15:15:13.098Z","target":"https://cyberchriz.github.io/musicto